      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before becoming Burr Ridge, the area was called Harvester, the site of International Harvester’s 1917 experimental farm that tested the first all‑purpose tractor, the Farmall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burr_Ridge%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1918 purchase of 300 acres by Chicago evolved into the Bridewell Prison Farm, which later became part of Burr Ridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
